
########## AI models (Pick model menu) ##########

Claude Haiku 4.5 – Fast, lightweight, good for summaries and simple Q&A.
Claude Opus 4.5 – Advanced reasoning, strong for complex logic and code review.
Claude Sonnet 4 – Balanced, good for general coding and explanations.
Claude Sonnet 4.5 – Improved Sonnet, better for programming and learning tasks.

Gemini 2.5 Pro – Google’s advanced model, strong for code, research, and multi-modal tasks.
Gemini 3 Flash (Preview) – Fast, lightweight, best for quick completions and chat.
Gemini 3 Pro (Preview) – More capable, good for programming and technical Q&A.

GPT-4.1 – Analytical, best for complex planning, multi-file changes, and careful code.
GPT-4o – Fast, high-quality, best for most coding (React, Django, DRF, API, auth, refactoring). Default for daily work.
GPT-5 – Deep reasoning, strong debugging, best for advanced frontend/backend and research.
GPT-5 mini – Extremely fast for boilerplate (CRUD, forms, test stubs, repetitive code). Use when speed is more important than depth.
GPT-5-Codex (Preview) – Code-focused, good for completions and code generation.
GPT-5.1 – Latest GPT-5, improved reasoning and code support.
GPT-5.1-Codex – Enhanced code generation, best for complex programming tasks.
GPT-5.1-Codex-Max – Maximum context and reasoning, for large codebases and deep analysis.
GPT-5.1-Codex-Mini (Preview) – Fast, economical, good for endpoints/components and multi-turn completions.
GPT-5.2 – Newest GPT-5, best for cutting-edge tasks and research.
GPT-5.2-Codex – Latest code-focused, for advanced programming and architecture.

Grok Code Fast 1 – Great for quick inline completions and small edits. Not ideal for big-picture or framework-specific work.
Raptor mini (Preview) – Use for docstrings, renames, or tiny fixes. Not for architecture or deep logic.

o1 (Advanced Reasoning) – For algorithms, architecture, or dense data-flow problems needing layered attention.
o1-mini – Lightweight, fast, and cost-effective for simple or repeated short prompts.

Best for most programming: GPT-4o (default), GPT-4.1, GPT-5.1-Codex, Claude Sonnet 4.5, Gemini 3 Pro.
Best for learning/experiments: Grok Code Fast 1, o1-mini, Raptor mini, Claude Haiku 4.5, Gemini 3 Flash.
Best for advanced/complex: GPT-5.2-Codex, GPT-5.1-Codex-Max, Claude Opus 4.5, o1 (Advanced Reasoning).

Tip: For most coding and learning, start with GPT-4o or Claude Sonnet 4.5. Switch to GPT-5.1-Codex, Gemini 3 Pro, or premium models for deep reasoning or critical code.

######## Mode Plan Github Copilot ################
The new "Plan" mode in GitHub Copilot is designed 
to assist developers with high-level planning and task breakdowns. Instead of focusing on code completions, this mode helps you:

Outline project structures:
    Create a roadmap or architecture for your project.
Break down tasks: 
    Suggest steps for implementing features or solving problems.
Generate documentation: Draft plans, workflows, or technical documentation.
    Collaborate on ideas: Provide structured suggestions for brainstorming or planning sessions.
It's particularly useful for project management, feature planning, and architectural decisions, complementing the coding-focused modes.